###Writing an equation

Let's substitute $\blueE{900}$ for $\blueE{\text{area}}$. Then, we can solve for $\goldE{\text{height }(h)}$ in terms of $\maroonD{\text{base }(b)}$:

$\begin{align}
\blueE{\text{area}}&=(\maroonD{\text{base}}) \cdot (\goldE{\text{height}})
\\\\
\blueE{900} &= \maroonD{b} \cdot \goldE{h}
\\\\
\dfrac{\blueE{900}}{\maroonD{b}} &= \goldE{h}
\\\\
\goldE{h} &= \dfrac{\blueE{900}}{\maroonD{b}}
\end{align}$

###Height when base is $25$ centimeters?

Let's use our equation to find the value of $\goldE{h}$ when $\maroonD{b}=\maroonD{25}$:

$\begin{align}
\goldE{h} &= \dfrac{\blueE{900}}{\maroonD{b}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\blueE{900}}{\maroonD{25}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{3{,}600}{100}
\\\\
&=36
\end{align}$
